e":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducable: Godot Engine 4.6 Stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable (89cea1439) - Freedesktop SDK 25.08 (Flatpak runtime) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 580 Series (RADV POLARIS10) - AMD Ryzen 5 3600 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 31.25 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen Adding a BoneTwistDisperser3D into a Skeleton, you can select the Root and End Bones, however the Field \"Reference Bone Name\" is greyed out and a bone cannot be selected. Typing into the field or pasting into it are also not an option. Without the bone set, the node seems non-functional. The Documentation does not describe what the Reference Bone Name is supposed to do or contain. \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Have a Skeleton3D node\n- Add a BoneTwistDisperser3D node to it\n- Add an entry to the settings\n- Observe the described state\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[MRP_BoneTwistDisperser3D.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24974298/MRP_BoneTwistDisperser3D.zip)\n\n<img width=\"404\" height=\"896\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b896761e-d9cc-46e4-ad2c-29fa4b15bea1\" />","closed_by":{"login":"MeisterLi","id":44271061,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MjcxMDYx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44271061?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeisterLi","html_url":"https://github.com/MeisterLi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeisterLi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeisterLi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MeisterLi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":